{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791203604,"nonce":"Q7oTJS1glkj5HNSEM9D5U3vZ238=","title":"LLVM alias tags leak across functions: GEP maps keyed by IrId never reset","message":"`gep_byte_offsets` and `gep_results` in llvm_jit_backend.rs (added bcad0a27, 2026-08-14) are keyed by IrId but were never cleared between functions, and every function numbers its IrIds from zero. Two effects:\n\n- A GEP whose base id was a GEP result in an earlier-compiled function is treated as GEP-off-GEP and gets no TBAA tag. Which accesses lose their tag depends on compile order and on the numbering of earlier functions.\n- A stale `gep_byte_offsets` entry can tag a load/store in a later function with another function's field offset (wrong TBAA, possible miscompile).\n\nSymptom: nbody under the tiered target. LLVM promotion (compile_llvm_bead -\u003e compile_functions) compiles main + callees in one backend; in the promoted `advance`, only 8/24 double loads and 3/9 stores were tagged before optimisation, so each store to a.vx/vy/vz could alias b.mass and the loop reloaded mass three times per pair and lost SLP vectorisation.\n\nBisect on the nuc (benchmark_runner nbody, runtime_min_ms, tiered):\n  fe45cf52 357 | 30015d6b 406 (select clamp) | 6113ac5e 398 | 0a345d88 484 (branch clamp changed IrId numbering) | e6838017 484\nThe llvm target compiles the whole module and was unaffected (362-378).\n\nFix A/B at e6838017, interleaved x3 (min ms): tiered 484/484/484 -\u003e 362/372/371; llvm 362-378 -\u003e 362; cranelift unchanged.\n\nSeparate, deliberate: Math.sqrt calls the runtime symbol from LLVM code (8df26dc0, store-forwarding rationale) — not part of this regression.","files":null}]}